Lefty has saved the day and has earned my undying respect....well, until
the next flame war at the very least.

His fix worked, and I am back to having my mail sorted properly.

His point that Eudora 1.4 *evilly* and *foolishly* modifies the "Settings"
file (Eudora doesn't use a conventional "Preferences" file) and then
doesn't put it back to what it was even when the earlier software (1.3) is
restored is the key.

My advice to Extropians: Stick with version 1.3, unless and until future
versions fix this situation. If you have already upgraded to 1.4fc1, you
have probably already seen the problem I've been describing. If so, go back
to 1.3 after trashing the "Settings" file (which may be in both the System
folder and your main Eudora folder).

However, be sure you have an *old* copy of your "Settings" file (before
having installed 1.4), as just trashing the current Settings file will
leave you with a brand new environment sans your old mailboxes and the
like. (There may be a way to recover or open mailboxes into a new
environment, but I don't know how. I was lucky to have saved a complete
copy of Eudora 1.3, including my old Settings file, so I was able to
restore my old environment.)

Lefty wrote, for reference:

>I bet you've upgraded your copy of Eudora in the interim.  I noticed this
>same thing when I upgraded to version 1.4.

