On the representationalist theory, it's difficult if not impossible to tell
the difference between percepts and concepts.  This theory leads to the
conclusion that concepts are merely complicated percepts, distinct merely
in quantity, not quality, and thus to the further conclusion that such is
the difference between man and beast.

