from one meaning to another as it suits you.  Until you provide a suitable
definition, consisting of genus and differentia, there's no point in my
trying to answer you about whether I do or do not claim anything at all
about anything "absolute."

2) In fact, you seem to have introduced the term itself merely in order to
confuse the issue, which seems to me like unprovoked hostility on your part.
Is it?  I'm perfectly content to leave it out.

3) What it all really comes down to is that you implicitly attack me for
what are ultimately methodological differences.  I'm quite willing to
acknowledge that I don't pretend to address the questions of social science
by the methods of physics, and furthermore, to defend my methods as those
indicated by the subject matter.  If you aren't willing to do the same for
your implicit claim that social science ought to be done the same way as
physics, then you have nothing relevant to say.

